From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH] clk: qcom: gcc-sm8350: keep the secondary USB GDSC in retention

The ROG Phone 5 runs its bottom USB-C port on the secondary controller
(usb_2) as a host. Once genpd switched usb30_sec_gdsc off, the controller
did not come back: a runtime resume logged "xHC error in resume, Reinit"
followed by an SMMU fault from SID 0x20 and "Host Controller Error", and a
fresh bind failed with "usb30_sec_gdsc status stuck at 'off'".

As done for the PCIe GDSCs (and like gcc-sm8450 for its USB GDSC), declare
it PWRSTS_RET_ON so genpd leaves it in retention instead of collapsing it.

--- a/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-sm8350.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-sm8350.c
@@ -3461,7 +3461,7 @@
 	.pd = {
 		.name = "usb30_sec_gdsc",
 	},
-	.pwrsts = PWRSTS_OFF_ON,
+	.pwrsts = PWRSTS_RET_ON,
 };
 
 static struct gdsc hlos1_vote_mmnoc_mmu_tbu_hf0_gdsc = {
